evolves with total energy availability E(t) = E_Earth(t) + E_Space(t). In Steady State 2, E_Space grows through solar power satellites and helium-3 fusion extraction from the lunar regolith, accelerating K_index at a rate proportional to the product of AI capability and space infrastructure precision (I_P). The Moon contains water ice that can be used to produce fuel and serves as a proving ground for technologies enabling deeper space exploration. [Atlasinstitute](https://atlasinstitute.org/the-future-of-the-space-economy/) The consequence is that the Kardashev trajectory under deliberate AI-surplus redirection reaches Type 1 by 2100–2150, rather than millennia hence under the business-as-usual path.

